      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im getting this SettingWithCopyWarning in my pandas notebook and its driving me crazy. i tried to do df[df['col'] > 5]['new_col'] = some_val but it keeps popping up. can u explain why this happens and how i should actually do it instead?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The `SettingWithCopyWarning` occurs in pandas when you're trying to assign a value to rows that may not be originally in the DataFrame, thus creating a potentially unintended copy of the DataFrame rather than modifying it in place. Instead, to modify the DataFrame safely, you should directly reference the original DataFrame by its name (in your case, `df`). To set values where `df['col'] > 5` and assign `some_val` to `new_col`, use the following syntax: `df.loc[df['col'] > 5, 'new_col'] = some_val`. This will perform the operation in place without raising a warning.",
